          "rule_title": "The application server management interface must retain the Standard Mandatory DoD Notice and Consent Banner on the screen until users acknowledge the usage conditions and take explicit actions to log on for further access.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the application server management interface to retain the logon banner on the screen until the user takes explicit action to logon to the server.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review application server management interface product documentation and configuration to determine that the logon banner can be displayed until the user takes action to acknowledge the agreement.\n\nIf the banner screen allows continuation to the application server without user interaction, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Application_Server_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "To establish acceptance of system usage policy, a click-through banner at the application server management interface logon is required. The banner shall prevent further activity on the application server unless and until the user executes a positive action to manifest agreement by clicking on a box indicating \"OK\".",
