          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: UDS owns authentication and already supplies the complete mandatory USGnotice plus acknowledgement UI. However its TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS required action is disabled by default and the release profile supplies no override. No custom API/banner implementation is needed; enable the existing provider action. Core ships the USG notice and acknowledgement UI; its terms action defaults off. Gallatin owns enabling the existing control. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply the same decision to similar notice/consent banner requirements. Share the existing V-222434/V-222435 configuration and verification actions, but verify the exact component and management entry points; Horizon login alone does not establish every platform entry path.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Verify current UDS notice/consent settings and inventory applicable interactive entry points for this exact component or management interface. Reuse V-222434/V-222435 configuration: persist the approved Core terms setting and update the existing realm through a controlled change if needed. Verify the required banner text and display before access. Verify the banner remains until explicit acceptance and users cannot proceed without acknowledgement. Test each applicable entry path, retain configuration/results and credit existing coverage. Do not create a duplicate Horizon banner or assume one login test covers all interfaces.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-appserver-release] re-appserver-release\nThe successful UDS push packaged2026.45.4-uds.1 records trusted Horizonb84b9af/build19710, packagecommitd528b7f, UDS Core 1.14.0 and platformContract identity.mode=uds, issuerhttps://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds. The actual delivered profile omits bundled Keycloak. Source-default bundled realm is not the delivered identity boundary.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-appserver-coreidentity] re-appserver-coreidentity\nCore 1.14 default enables OTP and X509, sets concurrent per-user limit0(unlimited), leaves inactivity workflow opt-in, includes explicit truststorepaths and optional alert enablement.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[re-appserver-realm] re-appserver-realm\nRealm provides X509UPN/custom-attribute mapping, OCSP checking defaulttrue/failclosed, localCRLfalse, OTP browser flow, user/admin events, ten-minute idle. Consent required action defaultsdisabled; inactivity workflow disabled unless configured; sessionsunlimited default.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-appserver-terms] re-appserver-terms\nUDS theme includes mandatory USG notice and explicit acknowledgement UI, but this template is reached only when the terms required action is enabled.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/theme/login/terms.ftl\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-banner] mpn-identity-banner\nShipped theme already contains USG InformationSystem notice/consent text and acknowledgementUI. Enable realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED=true; review mission applicability rather than build another banner.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/theme/login/terms.ftl\n\n[mpn-identity-init-only] mpn-identity-init-only\nrealmInitEnv and realmAuthFlows are initial realm import inputs. Existing realm is persisted in DB; redeploying Secret does not change it. Core documents equivalent Keycloak AdminConsole settings. Use controlled non-destructive AdminAPI/console update and persist the desired bundle override; do not advise tearing down production identity.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/identity-and-authorization/configure-keycloak-login-policies.mdx\n\n[mpn-core-known-identity-settings] mpn-core-known-identity-settings\nKnown Core settings: realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED and themeCustomizations.termsAndConditions.text.inline/configmap; realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER (default0 unlimited); realmInitEnv.X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED/RELATIVE_PATH/ABORT_IF_NON_UPDATED; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled(defaultfalse), logging.enabled/defaulttrue. These are Gallatin configuration choices.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml",
          "finding_details": "UDS owns authentication and already supplies the complete mandatory USGnotice plus acknowledgement UI. However its TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS required action is disabled by default and the release profile supplies no override. No custom API/banner implementation is needed; enable the existing provider action. Core ships the USG notice and acknowledgement UI; its terms action defaults off. Gallatin owns enabling the existing control. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply the same decision to similar notice/consent banner requirements. Share the existing V-222434/V-222435 configuration and verification actions, but verify the exact component and management entry points; Horizon login alone does not establish every platform entry path.\n\nNext action: Verify current UDS notice/consent settings and inventory applicable interactive entry points for this exact component or management interface. Reuse V-222434/V-222435 configuration: persist the approved Core terms setting and update the existing realm through a controlled change if needed. Verify the required banner text and display before access. Verify the banner remains until explicit acceptance and users cannot proceed without acknowledgement. Test each applicable entry path, retain configuration/results and credit existing coverage. Do not create a duplicate Horizon banner or assume one login test covers all interfaces."
