          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The build/release path verifies source image digests and produces archive hashes/provenance; image-based deployments provide a complete reproducible baseline and allow returning to a previous package. Tested database rollback is a separate operational requirement.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[images] Image release process\nBuilder verifies source digests and produces archive hashes; sample values with empty digests do not establish that a built release is unpinned. Assessed release/SBOM/scans still needed.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/scripts/build-bundle.py\n\n[app-namespace] app-namespace\nAll declared workload charts target horizon-uds; package supplies dedicated namespace, distinct workload charts and generated deployment credentials.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. The build/release path verifies source image digests and produces archive hashes/provenance; image-based deployments provide a complete reproducible baseline and allow returning to a previous package. Tested database rollback is a separate operational requirement.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
