          "group_id_src": "V-204744",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204744",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000142",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204744",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000142",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204744r1265171_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204744r1265171",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000142-AS-000014",
          "rule_title": "The application server must prohibit or restrict the use of nonsecure ports, protocols, modules, and/or services as defined in the PPSM CAL and vulnerability assessments.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the application server to disable any ports or protocols that are prohibited by the PPSM CAL and vulnerability assessments.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the application server documentation and deployment configuration to determine which ports and protocols are enabled.\n\nVerify that the ports and protocols being used are not prohibited and are necessary for the operation of the application server and the hosted applications.\n\nIf any of the ports or protocols is prohibited or not necessary for the application server operation, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Application_Server_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Some networking protocols may not meet organizational security requirements to protect data and components.\n\nApplication servers natively host a number of various features, such as management interfaces, httpd servers and message queues. These features all run on TCPIP ports. This creates the potential that the vendor may choose to utilize port numbers or network services that have been deemed unusable by the organization. The application server must have the capability to both reconfigure and disable the assigned ports without adversely impacting application server operation capabilities. For a list of approved ports and protocols, reference the DoW ports and protocols web site at https://public.cyber.mil/connect/ppsm/",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "V-57501",
            "SV-71777"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000382"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2900",
          "uuid": "e32e9c17-d826-5345-a508-7633efd82b2a",
          "stig_uuid": "3817652a-d733-5ebb-b7dc-03a0b4466071",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: UDS provides separate admin/tenant ingress, namespace default-deny and explicit per-package exposure/egress. Operators can remove exposure or disable identity to revoke access; exact approved MPN destinations are handled as the separate network-profile change.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-network] core-network\nOperator generates namespace ingress/egress default-deny NetworkPolicy; connectivity requires declared allow rules.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/pepr/operator/controllers/network/defaults/default-deny-all.ts\n\n[core-gateway] core-gateway\nGateway redirects HTTP to HTTPS and requires TLS 1.3 by default, optionally TLS 1.2; credentialName references Kubernetes TLS secrets.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/istio/charts/uds-istio-config/templates/gateway.yaml\n\n[mesh] Mesh and policy\nPackage chart declares ambient mesh and generated network policy. Disabled chart-local NetworkPolicy and plaintext application URLs do not establish missing mesh enforcement.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-uds-package/templates/package.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. UDS provides separate admin/tenant ingress, namespace default-deny and explicit per-package exposure/egress. Operators can remove exposure or disable identity to revoke access; exact approved MPN destinations are handled as the separate network-profile change.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204745",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204745",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000148",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204745",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000148",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204745r1265172_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204745r1265172",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000148-AS-000101",
          "rule_title": "The application server must use an approved DoW enterprise identity, credential, and access management (ICAM) solution to uniquely identify and authenticate users (or processes acting on behalf of organizational users).",
          "fix_text": "Configure the application server to use an approved enterprise ICAM solution to uniquely identify and authenticate users and processes acting on behalf of organizational users.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review application server documentation and configuration settings to determine if the application server is using an approved enterprise ICAM solution to authenticate organizational users and processes running on the users' behalf.\n\nIf an approved enterprise ICAM solution is not being used, this is a finding.\n\nNote: If the site is currently using an enterprise solution (AAA Server) and has documented their plans to move to an approved enterprise ICAM solution, the severity of this control can be reduced to a CAT III.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Application_Server_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "To ensure accountability and prevent unauthorized access, application server users must be uniquely identified and authenticated. This is typically accomplished via the use of a user store, which is either local (OS-based) or centralized (LDAP). However, DoDI 8520.03 now requires that applications use an approved DoW enterprise (E-ICAM) solution whenever the ICAM solution addresses information system needs. Where the ICAM solution has been evaluated and found to not meet the needs of information system owners, information system owners must reevaluate decisions to use locally managed solutions and transition to DoW enterprise ICAM solutions to the maximum extent possible as the enterprise ICAM solutions mature.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "V-35299",
            "SV-46586"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000764"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2900",
          "uuid": "7a85a74f-d8c6-5b41-88c2-f090fde06135",
          "stig_uuid": "3817652a-d733-5ebb-b7dc-03a0b4466071",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The delivered platformcontract explicitly selects centralized UDS enterpriseSSO and Horizon validates its configured issuer/audience/signed individualclaims. Credit the selected enterpriseICAMintegration; retain the platformapproval/inheritance record for final acceptance instead of implementing another application userstore.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain the delivered-release source mapping and component boundary in the checklist; no new application implementation is recommended for this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-appserver-release] re-appserver-release\nThe successful UDS push packaged2026.45.4-uds.1 records trusted Horizonb84b9af/build19710, packagecommitd528b7f, UDS Core 1.14.0 and platformContract identity.mode=uds, issuerhttps://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds. The actual delivered profile omits bundled Keycloak. Source-default bundled realm is not the delivered identity boundary.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-appserver-auth] re-appserver-auth\nEvery protected request validates OIDC claims and single tenantgroup, resolves stable sub->localuser/tenant, and sets trusted userId/tenantId CLS context. Pending/no-role users are denied.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/apps/api/src/api/auth/auth.guard.ts\n\n[re-appserver-coreidentity] re-appserver-coreidentity\nCore 1.14 default enables OTP and X509, sets concurrent per-user limit0(unlimited), leaves inactivity workflow opt-in, includes explicit truststorepaths and optional alert enablement.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[re-appserver-realm] re-appserver-realm\nRealm provides X509UPN/custom-attribute mapping, OCSP checking defaulttrue/failclosed, localCRLfalse, OTP browser flow, user/admin events, ten-minute idle. Consent required action defaultsdisabled; inactivity workflow disabled unless configured; sessionsunlimited default.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. The delivered platformcontract explicitly selects centralized UDS enterpriseSSO and Horizon validates its configured issuer/audience/signed individualclaims. Credit the selected enterpriseICAMintegration; retain the platformapproval/inheritance record for final acceptance instead of implementing another application userstore.\n\nNext action: Retain the delivered-release source mapping and component boundary in the checklist; no new application implementation is recommended for this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204746",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204746",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000149",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204746",
          "severity": "high",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000149",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204746r960972_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204746r960972",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000149-AS-000102",
          "rule_title": "The application server must use multifactor authentication for network access to privileged accounts.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the application server to authenticate privileged users via multifactor authentication for network access to the management interface.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the application server configuration to ensure the system is authenticating via multifactor authentication for privileged users.\n\nIf all aspects of application server web management interfaces are not authenticating privileged users via multifactor authentication methods, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Application_Server_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Multifactor authentication creates a layered defense and makes it more difficult for an unauthorized person to access the application server.  If one factor is compromised or broken, the attacker still has at least one more barrier to breach before successfully breaking into the target.  Unlike a simple username/password scenario where the attacker could gain access by knowing both the username and password without the user knowing his account was compromised, multifactor authentication adds the requirement that the attacker must have something from the user, such as a token, or to biometrically be the user.\n\nMultifactor authentication is defined as: using two or more factors to achieve authentication. \n\nFactors include: \n(i) something a user knows (e.g., password/PIN); \n(ii) something a user has (e.g., cryptographic identification device, token); or \n(iii) something a user is (e.g., biometric). A CAC or PKI Hardware Token meets this definition.\n\nA privileged account is defined as an information system account with authorizations of a privileged user.  These accounts would be capable of accessing the web management interface.\n\nWhen accessing the application server via a network connection, administrative access to the application server must be PKI Hardware Token enabled.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "V-35300",
            "SV-46587"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000765"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2900",
          "uuid": "9939a948-f8f4-5de4-84c4-ab9ed2cb0630",
          "stig_uuid": "3817652a-d733-5ebb-b7dc-03a0b4466071",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Horizondelegates authentication to actual UDS provider. Core chart renders OTP true into REQUIRED MFA/OTP flow, and provides X509/CAC path through the separateadmin/SSOgateway. A separate device OTP/CACpath is implemented at the identity layer; Horizon API does not need to repeat MFA after trusted OIDC authentication. Role/device policy exceptions remain platformconfiguration conditions.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain the delivered-release source mapping and component boundary in the checklist; no new application implementation is recommended for this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-appserver-release] re-appserver-release\nThe successful UDS push packaged2026.45.4-uds.1 records trusted Horizonb84b9af/build19710, packagecommitd528b7f, UDS Core 1.14.0 and platformContract identity.mode=uds, issuerhttps://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds. The actual delivered profile omits bundled Keycloak. Source-default bundled realm is not the delivered identity boundary.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-appserver-coreidentity] re-appserver-coreidentity\nCore 1.14 default enables OTP and X509, sets concurrent per-user limit0(unlimited), leaves inactivity workflow opt-in, includes explicit truststorepaths and optional alert enablement.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[re-appserver-flowrender] re-appserver-flowrender\nChart maps OTP_ENABLED=true to OTP_FLOW_ENABLED=REQUIRED and MFA_FLOW_ENABLED=REQUIRED, and maps X509 auth to enabled alternate flow. Raw realm interpolation fallbacks alone are not the final rendered flow.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/secret-kc-realm.yaml\n\n[re-appserver-realm] re-appserver-realm\nRealm provides X509UPN/custom-attribute mapping, OCSP checking defaulttrue/failclosed, localCRLfalse, OTP browser flow, user/admin events, ten-minute idle. Consent required action defaultsdisabled; inactivity workflow disabled unless configured; sessionsunlimited default.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-appserver-identitygateway] re-appserver-identitygateway\nUDS routes privateKeycloak paths away from public tenantgateway, exposes admin access separately, strips user-supplied clientcertificate header and injects downstreamcert for delegated X509 handling.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/uds-package.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Horizondelegates authentication to actual UDS provider. Core chart renders OTP true into REQUIRED MFA/OTP flow, and provides X509/CAC path through the separateadmin/SSOgateway. A separate device OTP/CACpath is implemented at the identity layer; Horizon API does not need to repeat MFA after trusted OIDC authentication. Role/device policy exceptions remain platformconfiguration conditions.\n\nNext action: Retain the delivered-release source mapping and component boundary in the checklist; no new application implementation is recommended for this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204747",
