        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204782",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204782",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000315",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204782",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000315",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204782r961278_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204782r961278",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000315-AS-000094",
          "rule_title": "The application server must control remote access methods.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the application server to enforce remote connection settings.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review organization policy, application server product documentation and configuration to determine if the system enforces the organization's requirements for remote connections.\n\nIf the system is not configured to enforce these requirements, or the remote connection settings are not in accordance with the requirements, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Application_Server_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Application servers provide remote access capability and must be able to enforce remote access policy requirements or work in conjunction with enterprise tools designed to enforce policy requirements.  Automated monitoring and control of remote access sessions allows organizations to detect cyber attacks and also ensure ongoing compliance with remote access policies by logging connection activities of remote users.\n\nExamples of policy requirements include, but are not limited to, authorizing remote access to the information system, limiting access based on authentication credentials, and monitoring for unauthorized access.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-71685",
            "V-57413"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-002314"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2900",
          "uuid": "e3933a1b-ea55-5acc-949b-e84bf0a3d88b",
          "stig_uuid": "3817652a-d733-5ebb-b7dc-03a0b4466071",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: UDS provides separate admin/tenant ingress, namespace default-deny and explicit per-package exposure/egress. Operators can remove exposure or disable identity to revoke access; exact approved MPN destinations are handled as the separate network-profile change.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-network] core-network\nOperator generates namespace ingress/egress default-deny NetworkPolicy; connectivity requires declared allow rules.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/pepr/operator/controllers/network/defaults/default-deny-all.ts\n\n[core-gateway] core-gateway\nGateway redirects HTTP to HTTPS and requires TLS 1.3 by default, optionally TLS 1.2; credentialName references Kubernetes TLS secrets.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/istio/charts/uds-istio-config/templates/gateway.yaml\n\n[mesh] Mesh and policy\nPackage chart declares ambient mesh and generated network policy. Disabled chart-local NetworkPolicy and plaintext application URLs do not establish missing mesh enforcement.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-uds-package/templates/package.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. UDS provides separate admin/tenant ingress, namespace default-deny and explicit per-package exposure/egress. Operators can remove exposure or disable identity to revoke access; exact approved MPN destinations are handled as the separate network-profile change.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204783",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204783",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000316",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204783",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000316",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204783r961281_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204783r961281",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000316-AS-000199",
          "rule_title": "The application server must provide the capability to immediately disconnect or disable remote access to the management interface.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the application server to have the capability to immediately disconnect or disable remote access to the management interface.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the application server product documentation and server configuration to ensure that there is a capability to immediately disconnect or disable remote access to the management interface.\n\nIf there is no capability, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Application_Server_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Without the ability to immediately disconnect or disable remote access, an attack or other compromise taking progress would not be immediately stopped.\n\nThe application server must have the capability to immediately disconnect current users remotely accessing the management interface and/or disable further remote access. The speed of disconnect or disablement varies based on the criticality of missions/business functions and the need to eliminate immediate or future remote access to organizational information systems.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
