          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: UDS provides separate admin/tenant ingress, namespace default-deny and explicit per-package exposure/egress. Operators can remove exposure or disable identity to revoke access; exact approved MPN destinations are handled as the separate network-profile change.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-network] core-network\nOperator generates namespace ingress/egress default-deny NetworkPolicy; connectivity requires declared allow rules.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/pepr/operator/controllers/network/defaults/default-deny-all.ts\n\n[core-gateway] core-gateway\nGateway redirects HTTP to HTTPS and requires TLS 1.3 by default, optionally TLS 1.2; credentialName references Kubernetes TLS secrets.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/istio/charts/uds-istio-config/templates/gateway.yaml\n\n[mesh] Mesh and policy\nPackage chart declares ambient mesh and generated network policy. Disabled chart-local NetworkPolicy and plaintext application URLs do not establish missing mesh enforcement.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-uds-package/templates/package.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. UDS provides separate admin/tenant ingress, namespace default-deny and explicit per-package exposure/egress. Operators can remove exposure or disable identity to revoke access; exact approved MPN destinations are handled as the separate network-profile change.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204784",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204784",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000340",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204784",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000340",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204784r961353_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204784r961353",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000340-AS-000185",
          "rule_title": "The application server must prevent non-privileged users from executing privileged functions to include disabling, circumventing, or altering implemented security safeguards/countermeasures.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the application server to deny non-privileged users access to and execution of privileged functions.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review application server documentation and configuration to verify that non-privileged users cannot access or execute privileged functions.\n\nHave a user logon as a non-privileged user and attempt to execute privileged functions.\n\nIf the user is capable of executing privileged functions, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Application_Server_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Preventing non-privileged users from executing privileged functions mitigates the risk that unauthorized individuals or processes may gain unnecessary access to information or privileges.\n\nRestricting non-privileged users also prevents an attacker, who has gained access to a non-privileged account, from elevating privileges, creating accounts, and performing system checks and maintenance.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "V-57399",
            "SV-71671"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-002235"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2900",
          "uuid": "aab706fc-a5cc-5fef-b586-1bb740f3bb93",
          "stig_uuid": "3817652a-d733-5ebb-b7dc-03a0b4466071",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Static assets and server configuration are in non-root/read-only containers; UDS blocks host access/privilege escalation and separates admin from tenant access. Application permission enforcement fails closed; native platform administration remains RBAC-controlled.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[app-pods] app-pods\nCandidate service chart applies non-root/read-only/no-escalation contexts, Secret references, probes and resource settings. Rendered app pods corroborate those settings; some init containers lack explicit resources.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-service/templates/deployment.yaml\n\n[core-policy] core-policy\nPepr mutates/validates non-root execution, no privilege escalation and dropped capabilities, including init and ephemeral containers; exemptions are explicit.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/pepr/policies/security.ts\n\n[app-web-image] app-web-image\nMultistage image copies only built Vue assets into the nginx runtime; source maps are removed. No application/OS user-management endpoint is implemented by the static nginx layer.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/3f3b51d454197c077b33896caf93de72b94eafda/apps/web/Dockerfile\n\n[app-enforcer] app-enforcer\nPermission enforcement resolves user/target and fails closed on missing authorization or unexpected resolution errors. Individual route metadata remains part of coverage.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/3f3b51d454197c077b33896caf93de72b94eafda/apps/api/src/core/authorization/permission-enforcer.service.ts",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Static assets and server configuration are in non-root/read-only containers; UDS blocks host access/privilege escalation and separates admin from tenant access. Application permission enforcement fails closed; native platform administration remains RBAC-controlled.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204785",
          "group_tree": [
            {
