          ],
          "group_id": "V-204792",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000371",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204792r981685_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204792r981685",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000371-AS-000077",
          "rule_title": "The application server must compare internal application server clocks at least every 24 hours with an authoritative time source.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the application server to compare internal application server clocks at least every 24 hours with an authoritative time source.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review application server documentation and confirm the application server compares internal application server clocks at least every 24 hours with an authoritative time source.\n\nIf the application server does not compare internal application server clocks to an authoritative source or if the frequency is greater than every 24 hours, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Application_Server_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Determining the correct time a particular application event occurred on a system is critical when conducting forensic analysis and investigating system events.\n\nSynchronization of system clocks is needed to correctly correlate the timing of events that occur across multiple systems. To meet this requirement, the organization will define an authoritative time source and have each system compare its internal clock at least every 24 hours.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-71707",
            "V-57435"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-004923"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2900",
          "uuid": "a7495f4e-a9d6-5269-9591-0a8899cd68ff",
          "stig_uuid": "3817652a-d733-5ebb-b7dc-03a0b4466071",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Containers inherit MPN node clocks; current application/server records have standard timestamps and the collection pipeline preserves them. Clock synchronization itself remains a host OS control with the specified comparison cadence.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[host] MPN ownership\nCurrent scope assigns control plane/node OS to MPN; no host assessment or live configuration was supplied.\nhttps://gallatin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GG/pages/733085804/WIP+STIG+SRG+Compliance+Scope+MPN\n\n[logging] API logging\nCurrent HTTP logger includes service, request/trace IDs, event, remote address and response status, with secret redaction. Its common bindings do not add authenticated actor identity; other records/correlation must be checked.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/3f3b51d454197c077b33896caf93de72b94eafda/apps/api/src/core/observability/logging.ts\n\n[core-id-audit] core-id-audit\nUDS event listener prints user/admin events to stdout with event fields and UTC timestamps. Vector can collect these without a separately configured app forwarding agent.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/plugin/src/main/java/com/defenseunicorns/uds/keycloak/plugin/eventListeners/JSONLogEventListenerProvider.java",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Containers inherit MPN node clocks; current application/server records have standard timestamps and the collection pipeline preserves them. Clock synchronization itself remains a host OS control with the specified comparison cadence.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
