          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000374-AS-000210",
          "rule_title": "The application server must record time stamps for log records that can be mapped to Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) or Greenwich Mean Time (GMT).",
          "fix_text": "Configure the application server to use time stamps for log records that can easily be mapped to UTC or GMT.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the application server documentation and configuration files to determine if time stamps for log records can be mapped to UTC or GMT.\n\nIf the time stamp cannot be mapped to UTC or GMT, this is a finding.",
