            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204808",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000404",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204808r981695_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204808r981695",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000404-AS-000249",
          "rule_title": "The application server must accept Federal Identity, Credential, and Access Management (FICAM)-approved third-party credentials.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the application server to accept FICAM-approved third-party credentials.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the application server documentation and configuration to determine if the application server accepts FICAM-approved third-party credentials.\n\nIf the application server does not accept FICAM-approved third-party credentials, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Application_Server_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Access may be denied to legitimate users if FICAM-approved third-party credentials are not accepted.\n\nThis requirement typically applies to organizational information systems that are accessible to non-federal government agencies and other partners. This allows federal government relying parties to trust such credentials at their approved assurance levels.\n\nThird-party credentials are those credentials issued by nonfederal government entities approved by the FICAM Trust Framework Solutions initiative.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-71795",
            "V-57519"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-004083"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2900",
          "uuid": "d6e09d7d-8dcb-5dd2-b205-64c54da36245",
          "stig_uuid": "3817652a-d733-5ebb-b7dc-03a0b4466071",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Actual delivered identity is UDS rather than bundled Keycloak. UDSaccepts X509 credentials at SSO/adminboundary, strips forgedcertificate headers, maps UPN/customcertificate attributes to individualusers, validates status viaOCSP and provisions SHA-verified DoD-approved externalPKItrust chains. This supplies PIV/CAC/partnerfederation mechanisms through delegatedidentity; the APIappropriately consumes its signed OIDC identity instead of parsing smartcards itself. Final approvedagency/profile scope is captured in the inheritance/trust record.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain the delivered-release source mapping and component boundary in the checklist; no new application implementation is recommended for this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-appserver-release] re-appserver-release\nThe successful UDS push packaged2026.45.4-uds.1 records trusted Horizonb84b9af/build19710, packagecommitd528b7f, UDS Core 1.14.0 and platformContract identity.mode=uds, issuerhttps://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds. The actual delivered profile omits bundled Keycloak. Source-default bundled realm is not the delivered identity boundary.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-appserver-coreidentity] re-appserver-coreidentity\nCore 1.14 default enables OTP and X509, sets concurrent per-user limit0(unlimited), leaves inactivity workflow opt-in, includes explicit truststorepaths and optional alert enablement.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[re-appserver-flowrender] re-appserver-flowrender\nChart maps OTP_ENABLED=true to OTP_FLOW_ENABLED=REQUIRED and MFA_FLOW_ENABLED=REQUIRED, and maps X509 auth to enabled alternate flow. Raw realm interpolation fallbacks alone are not the final rendered flow.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/secret-kc-realm.yaml\n\n[re-appserver-realm] re-appserver-realm\nRealm provides X509UPN/custom-attribute mapping, OCSP checking defaulttrue/failclosed, localCRLfalse, OTP browser flow, user/admin events, ten-minute idle. Consent required action defaultsdisabled; inactivity workflow disabled unless configured; sessionsunlimited default.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-appserver-identitygateway] re-appserver-identitygateway\nUDS routes privateKeycloak paths away from public tenantgateway, exposes admin access separately, strips user-supplied clientcertificate header and injects downstreamcert for delegated X509 handling.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/uds-package.yaml\n\n[re-appserver-trust] re-appserver-trust\nImage trust builder defaults officialDoD approved externalPKI trust chains ZIP, requires SHA256 verification, converts .cer files, excludes configured certificate categories, and includes non-expired certificates. This is actual source provisioning, not a generic claim that trust is unknowable.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/truststore/ca-to-jks.sh\n\n[re-appserver-trustsync] re-appserver-trustsync\nIdentityconfig sync copies generated certs into Keycloak conf/truststores and installs realm/plugin/theme configuration. FIPS libraries are copied when configured.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/sync.sh\n\n[re-appserver-auth] re-appserver-auth\nEvery protected request validates OIDC claims and single tenantgroup, resolves stable sub->localuser/tenant, and sets trusted userId/tenantId CLS context. Pending/no-role users are denied.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/apps/api/src/api/auth/auth.guard.ts",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Actual delivered identity is UDS rather than bundled Keycloak. UDSaccepts X509 credentials at SSO/adminboundary, strips forgedcertificate headers, maps UPN/customcertificate attributes to individualusers, validates status viaOCSP and provisions SHA-verified DoD-approved externalPKItrust chains. This supplies PIV/CAC/partnerfederation mechanisms through delegatedidentity; the APIappropriately consumes its signed OIDC identity instead of parsing smartcards itself. Final approvedagency/profile scope is captured in the inheritance/trust record.\n\nNext action: Retain the delivered-release source mapping and component boundary in the checklist; no new application implementation is recommended for this control."
        },
