          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Security flaws with software applications are discovered daily. Vendors are constantly updating and patching their products to address newly discovered security vulnerabilities. Organizations (including any contractor to the organization) are required to promptly install security-relevant software updates (e.g., patches, service packs, and hot fixes) to production systems after thorough testing of the patches within a lab environment. Flaws discovered during security assessments, continuous monitoring, incident response activities, or information system error handling must also be addressed expeditiously.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-71837",
            "V-57561"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-002605"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2900",
          "uuid": "1b53ee27-f6a4-5262-9d60-ad0811ea7805",
          "stig_uuid": "3817652a-d733-5ebb-b7dc-03a0b4466071",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The selected delivery is bound to a qualified successful main build with vendor FIPS image pins, automated advisory/update workflows and retained per-image scan records. Patch freshness can therefore be recommended from this delivered source/release evidence rather than left unknown for lack of a runtime command. This is date-bound; delivery source evidence is not a promise that an unseen operator installed future updates.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain release/scan dates and approved patch SLA; refresh this recommendation when the assessed release or advisory deadline changes.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-images-release] re-images-release\nSuccessful Nov5 trusted release2026.45.4-uds.1 binds Horizonb84b9af/build19710/run42109769948, package d528b7f, Core1.14.0, actual identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds. Twelve delivered image platform digests are explicit; no bundled Keycloak is shipped. Published package digest sha256:486f55939f94ab081d2a12ecade5439512f8f7c4b3119c40b027c711d386adc9. Read build-info/platform-contract/publication metadata artifact13464284834, not just example chart defaults.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-images-compose] re-images-compose\nActual selected source pins node-fips24.22.1-slim@b61e57c2..., nginx-fips1.31.8@72d1e862..., postgres-fips18.6@9760ae95..., python-fips3.13.18; release runtimeSource binds exact platform manifests and PostgreSQL source/build definition.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/compose.yml\n\n[re-images-scans] re-images-scans\nActual qualified run42109769948 succeeded per-image Grype/SBOM and ClamAV jobs, with retained API/web reports; reused PostgreSQL has its own verified prior build/scan evidence. Weekly dependency security-update automation exists. Release packaging scans have a narrower scope than source and application-image scans.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/.github/workflows/build.yml\n\n[re-images-maintained] re-images-maintained\nVendor states FIPS product variants are maintained with daily rebuilds and CVE SLA. Selected delivery is Nov5 (five days before this review) with explicit supported product versions and recent scan records, rather than an unknown model-server implementation substituted for delivered products.\nhttps://www.chainguard.dev/docs/platform/fips/fips-images",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. The selected delivery is bound to a qualified successful main build with vendor FIPS image pins, automated advisory/update workflows and retained per-image scan records. Patch freshness can therefore be recommended from this delivered source/release evidence rather than left unknown for lack of a runtime command. This is date-bound; delivery source evidence is not a promise that an unseen operator installed future updates.\n\nNext action: Retain release/scan dates and approved patch SLA; refresh this recommendation when the assessed release or advisory deadline changes."
        },
