          "finding_details": "Audit coverage is partially implemented. Successful grant/revoke operations already have append-only actor-attributed permission audit records and IdP admin actions have separate UDS logging. The remaining concrete application-domain gap is unsuccessful/denied privilegeaccess or mutation: the guard returns403 without recording actor, while transaction/precondition failures can occur before audit insert or roll it back. Generic HTTPstatus records do not recover that missing actor. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply the partially implemented recommendation to similar audit-coverage requirements. Confirm required controls, credit existing coverage and implement only the missing required event coverage; this is not a final compliance finding.\n\nNext action: Add narrowly-scoped actor-attributed denied/failed privilege events and forward them through the existing logging path; reuse existing successful audit. As part of the shared V-222431 audit-control review, confirm the required event catalog for this exact requirement, map existing coverage, implement missing desired controls consistent with the STIG minimum, and retain verification evidence. Preserve scoped applicability decisions for nonexistent operations."
