string-key/string-value tags; file PUT/PATCH/output schemas preserve tags. Existing object metadata can carry approved privacy-purpose labels without introducing a parallel per-object metadata table.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/apps/api/src/api/files/files.schema.ts\n\n[re-mission-ingestion-tags] re-mission-ingestion-tags\nIngestion copies caller tags into resolved_tags and passes classification/tags to persisted jobs and downstream chunk preparation. This supports propagation of approved metadata but does not itself define legal processing purposes or field-level PII scope.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/workers/artifact-ingestion/artifact_ingestion/processor.py\n\n[re-docs-classification-policy] re-docs-classification-policy\nCompany data-classification guidance exists; contract-specific applicable CUI categories and approved systems by tier remain explicit decision inputs. This is distinct from source-level classification enums or enforcement mechanisms and does not justify claiming no taxonomy exists.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/gallatin-company-policies/blob/e5b6ec5a2862cc3880c2ccc011d57698f14611e9/POL-CUI-data-classification.md",
          "finding_details": "The candidate PII elements are identifiable in the delivered identity schema, and file/chunk tag propagation already exists. The missing processing purposes association is a bounded policy/configuration integration, not a reason to invent a new general tagging subsystem. Tenant_id and security classification do not encode this semantic purpose by themselves.\n\nNext action: Have the privacy/mission data owner approve the PII element/purpose matrix below. Reuse files.tags and propagated chunk metadata for document-level tags such as privacy.profile, privacy.authorized_processing and privacy.processing_purpose. Attach a versioned schema-level privacy profile to account identity fields in the API/schema data dictionary; implement and validate only the missing association/propagation needed by the approved scope. If field-level tags are required, add narrow schema metadata or a field-to-policy mapping, not a wholesale per-row schema rewrite. Verify the exact data-tag interpretation with the assessor before treating a standalone document as an attached tag."
