          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-003376"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2900",
          "uuid": "ffbdf340-6b1d-5424-846f-aa55c761301e",
          "stig_uuid": "3817652a-d733-5ebb-b7dc-03a0b4466071",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The selected package binds maintained UDS Core1.14.0, current vendor FIPS runtimes and a successful qualified Horizon main release with actual support/update pipelines. Delivered API/web SBOM versions and vendor maintenance are known. An unselected future local model server should get its own component assessment, not keep all currently delivered products vendor-support unknown.\n\nComponents: Delivered Horizon API, workers, chat, ingestion and storage; delegated UDS identity/gateway/mesh\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain selected product support inventory; separately assess any newly selected local model runtime.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-images-release] re-images-release\nSuccessful Nov5 trusted release2026.45.4-uds.1 binds Horizonb84b9af/build19710/run42109769948, package d528b7f, Core1.14.0, actual identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds. Twelve delivered image platform digests are explicit; no bundled Keycloak is shipped. Published package digest sha256:486f55939f94ab081d2a12ecade5439512f8f7c4b3119c40b027c711d386adc9. Read build-info/platform-contract/publication metadata artifact13464284834, not just example chart defaults.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-images-compose] re-images-compose\nActual selected source pins node-fips24.22.1-slim@b61e57c2..., nginx-fips1.31.8@72d1e862..., postgres-fips18.6@9760ae95..., python-fips3.13.18; release runtimeSource binds exact platform manifests and PostgreSQL source/build definition.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/compose.yml\n\n[re-images-api-sbom] re-images-api-sbom\nActual built API SBOM contains nodejs24.22.1-r2, NIST-CMVP-5132, openssl-provider-fips-3.4.0 version3.4.0-r5, openssl-config-fipshardened4.1.0-r0. NIST-CMVP-5523-optin is also present but is not the default provider.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/actions/runs/42109769948/artifacts/13453332302\n\n[re-images-web-sbom] re-images-web-sbom\nActual web SBOM contains nginx-mainline1.31.8-r1, NIST-CMVP-5132, openssl-provider-fips-3.4.0-r5 and fipshardened configuration. Exact pinned base filesystem /etc/nginx/nginx.conf has worker_connections1024 and main log format with Referer, User-Agent and X-Forwarded-For; SHA256 bae65e6ef1d653fe5077c4c3dd66bcc6f6e8417ff1ae59825c9c2ae8bb2cb7b3. No live process execution needed.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/actions/runs/42109769948/artifacts/13455115354\n\n[re-images-pg-sbom] re-images-pg-sbom\nActual selected PostgreSQL build source9d3725b/run41699186459 SBOM contains postgresql18.6-r7, NIST-CMVP-5132, OpenSSL FIPS provider3.4.0-r5 and fipshardened configuration. The multistage extension copy deliberately excludes/reuses runtime libcrypto/libssl, preserving base module. Release verifies selected PostgreSQL definition/context hashes and exact platform digest3431665e....\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/actions/runs/41699186459/artifacts/13263507123\n\n[re-images-maintained] re-images-maintained\nVendor states FIPS product variants are maintained with daily rebuilds and CVE SLA. Selected delivery is Nov5 (five days before this review) with explicit supported product versions and recent scan records, rather than an unknown model-server implementation substituted for delivered products.\nhttps://www.chainguard.dev/docs/platform/fips/fips-images",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. The selected package binds maintained UDS Core1.14.0, current vendor FIPS runtimes and a successful qualified Horizon main release with actual support/update pipelines. Delivered API/web SBOM versions and vendor maintenance are known. An unselected future local model server should get its own component assessment, not keep all currently delivered products vendor-support unknown.\n\nNext action: Retain selected product support inventory; separately assess any newly selected local model runtime."
        }
